@@ -12,9 +12,25 @@ Usage
 -----
 
 ```go
-runewidth.StringWidth("つのだ☆HIRO") == 12
+runewidth.StringWidth("つのだ☆HIRO") == 11
 ```
 
+The star in that string is East Asian Ambiguous: one cell in most locales,
+two in a CJK one. The package-level functions use the width detected at
+startup from `LC_ALL`, `LC_CTYPE` and `LANG`, or from `RUNEWIDTH_EASTASIAN`
+when that is set, so the example above holds outside a CJK locale. To
+measure with the East Asian widths whatever the locale, use a condition:
+
+```go
+c := runewidth.NewCondition()
+c.EastAsianWidth = true
+c.StringWidth("つのだ☆HIRO") == 12
+```
+
+Assigning to the package-level `runewidth.EastAsianWidth` does not change
+what `runewidth.StringWidth` returns; it reports the detected locale and is
+read when a new `Condition` is built.
+
 
 Author
 ------
